# Packages allowed on an upgraded image only (verify-image.sh --upgraded):
# an image of an earlier release, or of Ubuntu 24.04, taken to this
# release as docs/install.md says. A new image does not have them.
# Format: <package> <reason>, as in allowlist.

# Ubuntu 24.04 to 26.04 (do-release-upgrade)
systemd-timesyncd       24.04's time daemon; Ubuntu's release upgrade keeps it (ubuntu-minimal and roxora-release depend on "chrony | time-daemon"), a new 26.04 image has chrony
gcc-14-base             24.04's GCC base package, marked manually installed in the 24.04 image (Armbian's package list), so the upgrade keeps it; on the ROCK 4D the GCC 14 of the DKMS toolchain still needs it
network-manager-l10n    recommended by network-manager on 26.04; the release upgrade installs new recommended packages, the image build installs network-manager without them
grub-common             UEFI image: needed by os-prober and grub2-common from the 24.04 image, which the upgrade keeps; a new 26.04 image has neither (as Ubuntu's 26.04 server image)
gnome-terminal          desktops: 24.04's terminal; 26.04's is Ptyxis, which the upgrade installs too, and Ubuntu's upgrade keeps gnome-terminal
gnome-terminal-data     data of gnome-terminal (above)

# Ubuntu 26.04 to 26.10 (do-release-upgrade)
dbus                    26.04's D-Bus system bus; 26.10 has dbus-broker, which the upgrade installs too; marked automatic and kept, as dbus-user-session, installed, accepts dbus-daemon
dbus-daemon             part of 26.04's D-Bus (above); dbus-user-session and dbus need it
libssl3t64              26.04's OpenSSL library (26.10 has libssl4), marked manually installed in the 26.04 image, so the upgrade keeps it; no installed package needs it
openssh-client-gssapi   26.10 splits GSSAPI out of openssh-client; the upgrade installs this package, which provides openssh-client with GSSAPI as 26.04's had it, marked manual; a new 26.10 image has openssh-client
selinux-utils           recommended by libselinux1 on 26.10; the release upgrade installs new recommended packages, the image build does not
